# k12 text report: the wmma + cp.async double buffer. Same tile as k14,
# so the same per-iteration design point (4096 tensor flops, 64 global
# bytes via cp.async, AI 64) and the same A100 machine line; the fragments
# come through wmma.load from shared (4 A x 16 B + 16 B x 16 B = 320 B).
# The loop's guard `K + 15 > 30` tests its latch at k = 0, ⌊K/16⌋ > 0,
# so the loop is counted per execution of the guard: its tensor flops
# over the kernel are exact.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k12/k12.sm_80.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel void hgemm_double_buffer<128, 128, 16, 64, 64, 128>(
CHECK: loop with the most instructions (static): 12_double_buffer.cuh:114
CHECK: shared memory [static]: 16384 B per CTA
CHECK: loop 12_double_buffer.cuh:114 ($L__BB0_5)
CHECK: trips = param_2 / 16
CHECK: instructions = <= 98
CHECK: shared load 16 B                                        20
CHECK: {{  }}wmma.load.b.sync.aligned.row.m16n16k16.shared.f16     16
CHECK: {{  }}wmma.load.a.sync.aligned.row.m16n16k16.shared.f16      4
CHECK: tensor f16                                              16
CHECK: {{  }}wmma.mma.sync.aligned.row.row.m16n16k16.f32.f32       16
CHECK: tensor flops = 4096  (f16 4096)
CHECK: global bytes: load <= 64 B, store 0 B
CHECK: shared bytes: load 320 B, store <= 64 B
CHECK: AI(global) >= 64 flop/B
CHECK: totals [static]:
CHECK: tensor flops = 4096 * (param_2 / 16)  (f16 4096 * (param_2 / 16))
CHECK: unknowns: none
CHECK: coverage: instructions_classified 100.0%
CHECK: coverage: loop_trips_resolved 100.0% (1/1)
